<title>THAILAND: Ch Karnchang in Thai construction deal.</title>
<headline>Ch Karnchang in Thai construction deal.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thai construction firm Ch Karnchang Plc said on Friday its joint venture unit, JV BBCT Co Ltd, won a contract worth 12.5 billion baht ($480.77 million) to build and expand Thai expressways.</p>
<p>The contract was signed on Thursday between JV BBCT, in which Ch Karnchang has a 59.98 percent stake, and expressway operator Bangkok Expressway Plc, the firm said in an advisory to the Stock Exchange of Thailand. No other details were given.</p>
<p>The other major partner in JV BBCT is Germany's Bilfinger UND Berger Bauaktiengesellschaft which holds a 40 percent interest in the joint venture unit.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
